<Layout title="About RAW vs JPEG: Our Camera Sample Project" description="Learn why RAW vs JPEG publishes original sample links, reproducible processing methods and transparent storage calculations.">
<article class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THIS PROJECT</p><h1>About RAW vs JPEG</h1><p>RAW vs JPEG is an independent, open-source camera-file comparison and storage planning project. We make it easier to understand what a RAW sample contains, what its camera preview looks like, and what keeping those files may cost in storage.</p><h2>What we measure</h2><p>We publish original RAW file byte sizes, source links and checksums. Our current examples come from public CC0 camera files in raw.pixls.us; the JPEG sides are embedded previews, not independently captured JPEG files. We do not present single samples as camera averages or claim controlled exposure recovery.</p><h2>Who maintains it?</h2><p>The project is maintained through the public <a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/raw-vs-jpeg">COLDDCC/raw-vs-jpeg repository</a>. An author biography, portrait and personal camera experience have not yet been supplied, so we do not invent them.</p><h2>Methods and corrections</h2><p>Review our <a href="/methodology/">reproducible method</a> or <a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/raw-vs-jpeg/issues">report an error through GitHub Issues</a>. You can also <a href="/cameras/">browse measured camera files</a>.</p></article></Layout>